=== 1. is either unreached act obtainable WITHOUT the unset bit? ===
  RESHAPE            rules  17/256; of those, 0 have NOTWIN CLEAR -> REQUIRES NOTWIN
  AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR   rules  15/256; of those, 7 have SELF CLEAR -> obtainable without it
      e.g. [(24, 'NOTWIN+HIDDEN'), (40, 'NOTWIN+CAPPED'), (56, 'NOTWIN+HIDDEN+CAPPED'), (72, 'NOTWIN+REFUTED'), (88, 'NOTWIN+HIDDEN+REFUTED'), (104, 'NOTWIN+CAPPED+REFUTED')]

=== 2. ruling surface each never-set bit gates ===
  NOTWIN  flips the ruling on  47 of 128 base situations; acts reachable ONLY once NOTWIN can be set: ['AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR', 'RESHAPE']
  SELF    flips the ruling on   2 of 128 base situations; acts reachable ONLY once SELF can be set: none
      x=  7 BUILT+AMB+UNREAD         ADD_STATE              -> with SELF: RAISE_BUDGET
      x=  8 NOTWIN                   RESHAPE                -> with SELF: AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR

=== 3. marginal value of making one bit measurable, from today's 9 ===
  (new situations = today's 9 with the bit added, minus the 9)
  today: 9 situations -> acts ['ADD_MATERIAL', 'ADD_STATE', 'CHANGE_GRANULARITY', 'HARVEST_COUNTEREXAMPLE', 'RAISE_BUDGET', 'SHIP']
  +BUILT    -> + 4 situations, new acts: none
  +AMB      -> + 7 situations, new acts: none
  +UNREAD   -> + 7 situations, new acts: none
  +NOTWIN   -> + 9 situations, new acts: ['AUTHOR_SUCCESSOR', 'RESHAPE']
  +HIDDEN   -> + 7 situations, new acts: none
  +CAPPED   -> + 3 situations, new acts: none
  +REFUTED  -> + 5 situations, new acts: none
  +SELF     -> + 9 situations, new acts: none

